    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d700">

                <pb facs="0792" n="672" xml:id="pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/420: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-14T12:00:00+01:00">February 14,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 14—-6:58 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>31. Consulate’s 19, January 23, 9 p.m., paragraph 2, and despatch No. 60,
                    political, February 5.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d700-f1"/> Liberia has informed
                    Secretary General that Council’s pertinent recommendation has been complied with
                    by Liberia’s ratification of Convention on Forced Labor of 1930, Instrument of
                    ratification not yet deposited.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
